		<section name="node">
			<attribute key="id" type="int">80</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">Following is what I came up with.
1. Create 2 variables, altitude and valleyCount and initialize them to 0
2. Take a step from the trek
3. If it is U, increment the altitude
4. Otherwise,
4.1 Decrement the altitude
4.2 If altitude is -1, that means we entered a valley. Increment the valleyCount
5. Repeat steps 2 to 4, until we reach the end of the trek
6. The value of valleyCount will be the number of valleys in the given trek
7. Repeat steps 1 to 6, for each of the test cases</attribute>
			<section name="graphics">
				<attribute key="x" type="double">6972.821031746032</attribute>
				<attribute key="y" type="double">2493.960800724026</attribute>
				<attribute key="w" type="double">319.47475971991173</attribute>
				<attribute key="h" type="double">213.6455758623414</attribute>
				<attribute key="type" type="String">rectangle</attribute>
				<attribute key="raisedBorder" type="boolean">false</attribute>
				<attribute key="fill" type="String">#FFCC00</attribute>
				<attribute key="outline" type="String">#000000</attribute>
			</section>
			<section name="LabelGraphics">
				<attribute key="text" type="String">Following is what I came up with.
1. Create 2 variables, altitude and valleyCount and initialize them to 0
2. Take a step from the trek
3. If it is U, increment the altitude
4. Otherwise,
4.1 Decrement the altitude
4.2 If altitude is -1, that means we entered a valley. Increment the valleyCount
5. Repeat steps 2 to 4, until we reach the end of the trek
6. The value of valleyCount will be the number of valleys in the given trek
7. Repeat steps 1 to 6, for each of the test cases</attribute>
